SUMMARY:🍁🌿 Fall Hike: East Don Trail Adventure 🍪🥾
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n# **Toronto’s Newest Ravine Trai
 l\, Autumn Scenery & Fresh-Baked Cookies!**\n\nDid you join us for our las
 t East Don Trail adventure? People had such a great time\, and there was p
 lenty to talk about afterward! Now that fall is here\, we’re heading bac
 k to enjoy the trail in autumn.\nJoin us as we explore the **East Don Trai
 l**\, one of Toronto’s newest additions to its incredible ravine system.
 \n\nThis beautiful route follows the East Don River through peaceful fores
 ts\, wetlands\, and scenic valley landscapes\, connecting communities that
  were once separated.\nIf you’ve walked the Lower Don Trail\, this is a 
 different experience.\n\nExpect quieter pathways\, river views\, new bridg
 es\, and the feeling of discovering another corner of Toronto that many pe
 ople have yet to explore.\n\nMost of the route is paved and relatively eas
 y to walk. Just one warning: what goes down must come up! 😄\n\nThe fina
 l section includes a fairly steep hill\, so you should be comfortable tack
 ling a good climb near the end.\nAnd the best part? We’ll finish with a 
 couple of optional stops for coffee\, baked goods\, and cookies!\n\n## 
 🚶‍♂️ What We’ll Do\n\nWe’ll meet outside Broadview Subway Sta
 tion before making our way into the Don Valley to explore the East Don Tra
 il.\n\nAlong the way\, we’ll:\n🌿 Walk beside the East Don River\n🌉
  Cross bridges and follow scenic pathways\n🍂 Enjoy the ravine scenery a
 nd fall colours\n📸 Stop for photos and conversation\n☕ Visit Circles 
 & Squares Bakery Café near the end of the trail\n🍪 Continue to the Pea
 k Freans Cookie Outlet for discounted cookies and treats\n\n**Both stops a
 fterward are optional.** At Circles & Squares Bakery Café\, you can grab 
 a quick coffee or something baked\, or stay a little longer if you’d lik
 e. You’re welcome to join us for the cookie outlet afterward\, or make y
 our own plans.\n\nWe’ll finish at **Coxwell Subway Station via TTC bus**
 . This is a one-way walk\, so we will not be returning to Broadview Statio
 n.\n\n## 🍁 Weather & Expectations\n\nThis walk happens rain or shine un
 less severe weather makes it unsafe.\nThe trail is mostly paved and relati
 vely easy\, but there is one fairly steep hill near the end. Please come p
 repared for that final climb and wear comfortable walking shoes.\n\nThis i
 s a social walk\, not a guided historical tour. We’re here to enjoy the 
 scenery\, have conversations\, and explore one of Toronto’s newest green
  spaces together.\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meeting location:** 
 Outside Broadview Subway Station\n🦌 **Look for:** My Moose Hat!\n⏰ **
 Meeting time:** 11:00 AM\n🚶 **Departure:** 11:05 AM sharp. I’ll wait 
 a maximum of five minutes.\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\nPlease
  arrive on time\, as we’ll leave promptly.\n\n🏁 **End point:** Coxwel
 l Subway Station\, via TTC bus.\n\n## ☕🍪 After the Walk\n\n### First 
 stop: Circles & Squares Bakery Café\n\nWe’ll stop at **Circles & Square
 s Bakery Café** near the end of the trail. If you’d like\, grab a coffe
 e\, a pastry\, or something else from the bakery. This is a casual stop\, 
 so there’s no obligation to buy anything or stay for long.\n\n### Next s
 top: Peak Freans Cookie Outlet\n\nThen we’ll head to the **Peak Freans C
 ookie Outlet**\, where you can browse their selection of cookies\, cracker
 s\, and other treats at outlet prices.\nYou’re welcome to join us for bo
 th stops\, just one\, or head home after the hike. The choice is yours!\n\
 n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in person or by e-transfer to [mathewm
 aclean@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com).**\nThis fee helps s
 upport the group and allows us to continue organizing events like this. Th
 ank you for supporting our community! 💛\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n* 
 💧 Water\n* 👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n* 🧥 Weather-appropriate c
 lothing\n* 📱 A phone or camera for photos\n* 💵 Spending money if you
 ’d like coffee\, baked goods\, or cookies\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\
 nThis group is open to anyone who wants to be social and make friends\, wh
 ether single or partnered.\nWe also organize movies\, walks and hikes\, ar
 ts and culture outings\, restaurant gatherings\, and plenty more. There’
 s always something happening!\n\n## ⚠️ A Few Reminders\n\n* You’re w
 elcome to RSVP ahead of time or show up on the day if you’re unsure abou
 t your schedule.\n* Please keep an eye on the event page for updates in ca
 se plans change or the event needs to be cancelled.\n* Remember that this 
 is a one-way walk ending at Coxwell Subway Station\, not Broadview.\n\n
 👤 **Organized by Mathew**\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email *
 *[torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotm
 ail.com)**.\n\n**Come for Toronto’s newest trail.**\n**Stay for the coff
 ee and cookies.**\n**Leave having discovered another hidden corner of the 
 city.** 🍁🌿🍪
